  "notes": "Boot a Corvette ROM from an empty NVRAM with the coin door open (public 22 released); the scenario names no game. Leave the fresh-NVRAM FACTORY SETTINGS RESTORED loop with Escape (5), press Enter twice (game identification, then MAIN MENU), Up twice to T. TESTS and Enter to open the test menu at T.1 SWITCH EDGES. Run it with PinMAME's built-in race-car mechanisms enabled (--handle-mechanics 7), which hold each car's start switch at home and pulse its encoder while its enable output is on. Open T.17 RACE TEST, whose SELF TEST runs on entry and shows the LEFT/RIGHT START and POS (encoder) optos with the counted car positions; let it finish for 60 s, then select RESET, LEFT FORWARD and RIGHT FORWARD in turn with Up and hold Enter for 3 s on each, recording the race direction and enable outputs the ROM drives.",
